---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Medical & data disclaimer"
  description="What My Lab Tests is for, what it isn't, and the limits of the data we publish."
  path="/disclaimer/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Disclaimer', path: '/disclaimer/' }]}
>
  <div class="prose-tight max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold sm:text-3xl">Disclaimer</h1>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site — test explainers, FAQs, comparisons — is general
      information. It is not a diagnosis, a prescription, or a substitute for a
      doctor. Don't start, stop or change any treatment based on what you read
      here, and don't self-order tests to manage a condition without medical
      guidance.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Prices can move</h2>
    <p>
      Prices, fees, coupons and package contents are collected automatically
      from lab websites and re-checked on a schedule, but labs change them
      without notice. The lab's own checkout is always the final word. Every
      row shows the date we last verified it.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Bookings, sample collection, testing and reports are entirely between you
      and the lab you choose. Ratings displayed come from Google, the Play
      Store and the App Store and belong to those platforms.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Emergencies</h2>
    <p>
      If you're seriously unwell, skip the comparison shopping — call a doctor
      or get to a hospital.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
